  "notes": "Source: Albizu University Miami Campus Catalog (UPDATED February 28, 2026, official PDF), 'Bachelor of Business Administration in Behavioral Business and Innovation Technologies (On-Campus)' PROGRAM BREAKDOWN BY COURSE, hand-transcribed 2026-09-30 from the official PDF. Semester sequence is the collector's ordering (foundations first); the catalog does not print a term-by-term plan — advisor should confirm. Minimum 30 credits must be completed at the Miami Campus. Catalog presents Foundation (36 cr) + Major Concentration (36 cr) + three track areas: Psychology and Mental Health (18 cr), Emerging Technologies and Cybersecurity (15 cr), Leadership and Professional Development (15 cr). IMPORTANT CATALOG AMBIGUITY: the catalog labels these 'Track' without stating whether students choose one or complete all; the course breakdown sums to the catalog's stated 120-credit total only when all three tracks are counted (36+36+48=120), so all track courses are included here — confirm track selection with an advisor. Practicum/internship placement is required. Catalog quirk: BUS400 Capstone is printed without credit hours; 3 cr assumed (standard course value). Catalog prints 'English Composition II (pre-requisite ENC1101)' — transcribed as printed.",
